        "authorType": "COMMENT",
        "competitionRanking": 578,
        "content": "<p>As someone mentioned earlier, <strong>LLM inference is NOT deterministic</strong>, even with temp=0.0, hence the difference. Relevant blogs:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Defeating Nondeterminism in LLM Inference: <a href=\"https://thinkingmachines.ai/blog/defeating-nondeterminism-in-llm-inference/\" target=\"_blank\">https://thinkingmachines.ai/blog/defeating-nondeterminism-in-llm-inference/</a></li>\n<li>SGLang supports deterministic inference: <a href=\"https://www.lmsys.org/blog/2025-09-22-sglang-deterministic/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.lmsys.org/blog/2025-09-22-sglang-deterministic/</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.kaggle.com/ryanholbrook\" target=\"_blank\">@ryanholbrook</a> any chance the competition metric can be made deterministic?</p>",
        "feedbackTrackingData": {},
        "id": 3442946,
        "isThankYou": false,
        "kernelVersion": 0,
        "parent": {},
        "postDate": "2026-04-16T01:16:02.943Z",
