    "firstMessage": {
      "author": {
        "displayName": "Svanik Kolli",
        "id": 25849260,
        "progressionOptOut": false,
        "thumbnailUrl": "https://storage.googleapis.com/kaggle-avatars/thumbnails/25849260-kg.png?t=2026-04-21-18-23-19",
        "tier": "EXPERT",
        "url": "/svanikkolli"
      },
      "authorType": "TOPIC",
      "competitionRanking": 123,
      "content": "<p>I’ve noticed that when running Tong Hui Kang’s winning 0.85 submission zip, different people are reporting scores ranging from 0.84 to 0.86. Since the solution uses a temperature of 0.0 and a deterministic chain-of-thought, shouldn't the results be identical?</p>\n<p>I’m curious if anyone has identified the cause of this drift. Is it due to: </p>\n<p>Hardware differences (T4x2 vs Geforce RTX 6000 Pro) affecting floating-point operations?</p>\n<p>Discrepancies in vLLM versions or library environments?</p>\n<p>Slight misalignments between the original Tinker training and the Kaggle inference setup?</p>\n<p><img src=\"https://www.googleapis.com/download/storage/v1/b/kaggle-forum-message-attachments/o/inbox%2F25849260%2Fcbf1bcd95b29a79b8cce92e03148009b%2FScreenshot%202026-04-14%2011.18.59%20AM.png?generation=1776179955293601&amp;alt=media\" alt=\"\"></p>\n<p>Has anyone managed to consistently hit the 0.86 mark, and if so, did you make any environment tweaks to get there?</p>",
      "feedbackTrackingData": {},
      "id": 3441778,
      "isThankYou": false,
      "kernelVersion": 0,
      "parent": {},
      "postDate": "2026-04-14T15:19:31.843Z",
      "rawMarkdown": "I’ve noticed that when running Tong Hui Kang’s winning 0.85 submission zip, different people are reporting scores ranging from 0.84 to 0.86. Since the solution uses a temperature of 0.0 and a deterministic chain-of-thought, shouldn't the results be identical?\n\nI’m curious if anyone has identified the cause of this drift. Is it due to: \n\nHardware differences (T4x2 vs Geforce RTX 6000 Pro) affecting floating-point operations?\n\nDiscrepancies in vLLM versions or library environments?\n\nSlight misalignments between the original Tinker training and the Kaggle inference setup?\n\n![](https://www.googleapis.com/download/storage/v1/b/kaggle-forum-message-attachments/o/inbox%2F25849260%2Fcbf1bcd95b29a79b8cce92e03148009b%2FScreenshot%202026-04-14%2011.18.59%20AM.png?generation=1776179955293601&alt=media)\n\nHas anyone managed to consistently hit the 0.86 mark, and if so, did you make any environment tweaks to get there?",
